<title>USA: U.S. daily aluminum output up slightly in June.</title>
<headline>U.S. daily aluminum output up slightly in June.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Average daily primary aluminum output in the United States rose slightly to 9,872 tonnes in June, compared with 9,819 tonnes in May and 9,765 tonnes in June 1996, the U.S. Aluminum Association said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Total output in June was 296,170 tonnes, compared with 304,394 tonnes in May and 292,944 tonnes in June last year.</p>
<p>Output so far this year is 1,785,806 tonnes compared with 1,776,825 tonnes in 1996. The annual rate of production in June was 3,603,402 tonnes compared with an annual rate of 3,583,994 tonnes in May and 3,573,917 tonnes in June 1996.</p>
<p>((New York Commodity Desk 212-859-1646))</p>
